0..75 Comment "// Transport along a path between types built from an equivalence, the HoTT"
76..151 Comment "// book\'s § 2.10 (`ua`) and Lemma 2.10.5 (transport along `ua(e)` is `e`),"
152..227 Comment "// in the family of lists: negation, its own inverse, makes a path from the"
228..302 Comment "// booleans to themselves, and transport along it negates every element. A"
303..377 Comment "// pair of maps whose round trips differ makes no path, and an equivalence"
378..444 Comment "// between types of lists is out of the stratum `equiv` certifies."
446..491 Comment "// Negation and the identity on the booleans."
